cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "On the Local Commutation Limits of Phase-Modulated Sieve Operators"
authors:
  - family-names: "Frohman"
    given-names: "Benjamin Stanley"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7068-3718"
    email: "frohmanbenjamin@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Texas, United States"
type: article
abstract: >-
  A no-go result: phase-modulated contour operators built from truncated
  prime-factor counts, with a phase depending only on a fixed modulus
  (42/208), cannot isolate twin primes. Embedding Selberg weights commutes
  and does not raise Maynard's ρ. The established unconditional bound
  remains H₁ ≤ 246. This work does not claim an improvement on that bound.
keywords:
  - "sieve theory"
  - "parity problem"
  - "Maynard-Tao weights"
  - "twin primes"
  - "no-go"
